# Exclude from Docker build context — keeps builds fast, secrets out
# Without this, all files are uploaded to the Docker daemon before the build starts (slow + leaks .env)
# docker build .
#   Step 1: Upload ALL files to daemon        ← .dockerignore controls this
#   Step 2: Dockerfile COPY picks from them   ← only these go into the image

#   Without .dockerignore: 200MB uploaded, but only 6KB actually copied into image
#   With .dockerignore:    6KB uploaded, 6KB copied into image

#   The image is the same size either way (assuming specific COPY commands). The upload is what's wasteful.
node_modules
.git
.env
dist
README.md
